---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const running = 8;
const stopped = 4;
---

<Page
  path="/host/"
  title="Host | kiln-vm"
  description="kiln-vm needs one Linux host with KVM on amd64 or arm64. kiln-vm doctor checks the host before you create anything."
>
  <Fragment slot="open">
    <div class="say open">
      <div class="say__lead">
        <h1 class="say__title">Host</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="say__text">
        kiln-vm is a daemon, <code>kiln-vmd</code>, and a CLI that talks to it. The daemon runs on one Linux machine,
        keeps its state under <code>/var/lib/kiln-vm</code> and listens on <code>127.0.0.1:5456</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <section class="plate plate--slab needs">
    <div class="say">
      <div class="say__lead">
        <h2 class="say__title">What it needs</h2>
        <pre class="cmd">kiln-vm doctor</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="say__text">
        A Linux host on amd64 or arm64 with <code>/dev/kvm</code>. <code>doctor</code> checks KVM, Firecracker, the
        guest kernel and the host tools, and warns when disk or memory is short.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="form form--sunk kvm" aria-hidden="true">/dev/kvm</p>
  </section>

  <section class="plate plate--panel">
    <div class="say">
      <div class="say__lead">
        <h2 class="say__title">How much it runs</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="say__text">
        By default a host runs 8 VMs at a time, sharing 8 vCPUs and 8192 MB of memory. Stopped VMs use none of that,
        so you can keep more than you run.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="rack" aria-hidden="true">
      {Array.from({ length: running }, () => <span class="rack__on" />)}
      {Array.from({ length: stopped }, () => <span class="rack__off" />)}
    </div>
  </section>
</Page>

<style>
  .open {
    padding-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 4rem);
  }

  .needs {
    padding-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem);
  }

  .kvm {
    --fit: 5.58;
    --bearing: 0.031em;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-bottom: 0;
  }

  .rack {
    display: flex;
    gap: clamp(0.375rem, 1.1cqw, 1.25rem);
    height: clamp(7rem, 24cqw, 26rem);
  }

  .rack span {
    flex: 1;
  }

  .rack__on {
    background: var(--rib), var(--moulded);
  }

  .rack__off {
    background: var(--rib), linear-gradient(180deg, rgb(10 24 56 / 0.2), rgb(10 24 56 / 0.07) 78%);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 0 #ffffff;
  }
</style>
